 "caveats": [
  {
   "title": "No Chapter 5 section; the fault codes are the procedure",
   "text": "Chapter 5's component-level sections run §5-4 to §5-23 and stop at A18. For this board the published procedure is fault codes 3700 to 3705 and 3708, all of which test the 82C55 U14 or the DUART U5, plus the theory in §2-204 to §2-214. A dead GPIB, serial port or 5725A link raises no code at all; those are worked from the sheets."
  },
  {
   "title": "Two revisions with different stock numbers for the same parts",
   "text": "Fourteen rows of the Rev 9 list carry stock numbers the 1996 list does not: every carbon-film resistor (R3-R10, R20 in the 573xxx series against the 1996 list's 348xxx and 441xxx), R1, C8, CR1-CR4, U6, U7 and VR1/VR2. They are the same parts renumbered, and joined by designator, so each shows its 1996 row with the Rev 9 row as the as-built alternative. C71, CR5, CR6, R22 and R23 exist only in the 1996 list -- added after Rev 9 -- and so have no manufacturer part number."
  },
  {
   "title": "Test points are parts-list rows",
   "text": "TP1-TP15 appear in Table 6-27 as 'JUMPER,WIRE,NONINSUL,0.200CTR', stock 816090, quantity 15 -- the same purchased wire loop as A7's E-links. They are real probe targets; their nets are named only in the sheet 1 legend."
  },
  {
   "title": "No values are published for the board's own nodes",
   "text": "The supply test points carry the bands of the tables that generate them (A19's Table 2-2, A17's Table 2-10) and are marked inferred; the serial lines and PA COM have no published value. A rail out of band here is checked at its source assembly before anything on this board."
  },
  {
   "title": "No photograph",
   "text": "No photograph of the rear panel board exists in this project, so the photo, overlay and swipe display modes have nothing to show."
  },
  {
   "title": "§2-212 names R18 and R19, which the board does not have",
   "text": "The theory says the BNC shell connections are protected by resistors R18 (J5) and R19 (J6). Neither appears in Table 6-27, on the locator or on sheet 4; in their places are the 0.25 A fuses F1 and F2. The description predates the change; the fuses are what to check."
  },
  {
   "title": "K12 means two things",
   "text": "K12 on this board switches the VARIABLE PHASE OUT BNC. §2-213 also says U17 'creates control line RLY12* which controls relay K12 on the Analog Motherboard assembly (A3)' -- a different relay on a different board, driven from here."
  },
  {
   "title": "Designators on the sheets that are not in the parts list",
   "text": "Sheet 2 draws S2, an 'UNUSED SWITCH' beside the CALIBRATION switch S1; sheet 4 draws P11 and P12 (the mates of J11 and J12) and the two boost cable terminals TB1 and TB2. None of them is in Table 6-27 or on the locator, so none is a part in this dataset."
  }
 ],
